    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed and why it satisfies the spec:\n\n## What changed\n\n**`HouseholdDuplicates.java`** (small, self-contained helper)\n- `householdId(owner)` now computes the **deterministic** id: first **12 hex chars** of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (was 8 bytes over lastName + address).\n- `assignHousehold(...)` now **always** stamps the computed id on every owner (previously only when `sharesHousehold`). So owners with the same lastName+postcode share it automatically.\n- `isRejectedDuplicate(...)` (previously dead code) now rejects when an existing owner is in the same computed household, unless `sharesHousehold` is set \u2014 this is the 409 household-duplicate block that `sharesHousehold` bypasses.\n\n**`PossibleDuplicates.java`**\n- `matchId(...)` now keys off the **computed householdId** instead of raw lastName+postcode, and returns `null` for a **declared member** (`sharesHousehold`) \u2014 \"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** (the big class \u2014 kept edits minimal)\n- Added one clause to the existing conflict `if` for `HouseholdDuplicates.isRejectedDuplicate(...)`.\n- Passed `sharesHousehold` through to `PossibleDuplicates.matchId(...)`.\n\n## Behavior against the spec\n- householdId is deterministic from (normalizedLastName, postcode); same \u2192 shared id, different lastName \u2192 different id (exactly what the new test asserts). \u2705\n- `sharesHousehold` no longer creates the link (id is always computed); it only bypasses the duplicate block. \u2705\n- A second owner with the same lastName+postcode \u2192 409, unless `sharesHousehold` \u2192 created as a declared member and **not** flagged as a possible duplicate. \u2705\n- Duplicate detection (`IdentityKey`/`PossibleDuplicates`) and the household-size formula both key off the deterministic `household_id`. \u2705\n\n## Structural impact\nOnly the controller's `addOwner` was touched in a large class, and just ~3 changed lines there (line 108's call kept its signature to avoid an edit). The behavioral logic lives in the two tiny helper classes (`HouseholdDuplicates`, `PossibleDuplicates`), each with near-zero surrounding complexity. I left the OpenAPI docs and `Owner`/mapper untouched since the deterministic `household_id` column already feeds the existing `householdSize` formula.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
